From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jica98 <jica.etzc@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:40:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] nir/opt_load_store_vectorize: use upper bound of the base
 in robustness check

If the base offset of the low access cannot overflow when adding the
distance to the high access, combining them cannot change which accesses
are considered out of bounds.

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_load_store_vectorize.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_load_store_vectorize.c b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_load_store_vectorize.c
index e71d43c9..98ea5ac8 100644
--- a/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_load_store_vectorize.c
+++ b/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_load_store_vectorize.c
@@ -1441,6 +1441,13 @@ check_for_robustness(struct vectorize_ctx *ctx, struct entry *low, uint64_t high
    if (low->info->base_src < 0)
       return true;
 
+   nir_def *base = low->intrin->src[low->info->base_src].ssa;
+   if (base->bit_size == 32 && base->num_components == 1 &&
+       high_offset <= UINT32_MAX &&
+       !nir_addition_might_overflow(ctx->shader, &ctx->uub_ht,
+                                    nir_get_scalar(base, 0), high_offset))
+      return false;
+
    /* Second, use information about the factors from address calculation (offset_defs_mul). These
     * are not guaranteed to be power-of-2.
     */
